  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-11",
  "question": "Which costs require fewer mounted nodes, and what selection, find and export guarantees survive partial DOM coverage?",
  "model": "GPT-6 / Codex",
  "method": "best-api/design-v1; history-v2",
  "trigger": "User requested $task design large-documents: make DOM omission explicit and consolidate rendering modes.",
  "requirements": [
    "One truthful ordinary DOM-present editing contract and an explicit product opt-in to omission.",
    "Preserve exact mounted root/view, selection, input/composition, clipboard and layout authority.",
    "Choose concrete raw, Plate and pagination call shapes with contextual inference and complete bounded owner dispositions.",
    "Runtime, geometry and packaging consolidation remain provisional without a passing source-bound executable comparison."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "The initial review matched at design intake. Reused its static default/coverage trace and historical performance limits, then expanded to complete public imports, pagination positioning and package dependency reachability. The current design corrects a diagnostic-only metrics assumption after tracing its real pagination positioning consumer.",
  "summary": "Specify virtualize on the existing Editable and privately normalize pagination layout; remove strategy taxonomy, automatic segments, staged retention and public metrics/offset protocols. Defer runtime, geometry and packaging acceptance: source drift and incomplete probe coverage prevent a passing comparison.",
  "verdict": "defer",
  "previous": "2026-09-11-large-documents-explicit-dom-coverage",
  "relation": "defers",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep/configure: existing full is a control, not a durable requirement for every application to repair the default.",
    "Change API: select proposed virtualize boolean/options on the existing Editable; Plate inherits it and PagedEditable supplies measured layout privately. The compile-only caller sketch passes.",
    "Add primitive: no public window store, virtualizer factory or search service. One committed root DOM marker serves the existing copied pagination CSS job without metrics-to-state feedback.",
    "Delete/merge: remove strategy taxonomy, automatic segment/staged owners, public layout arrays, find metadata and diagnostics. Pagination metrics removal is gated on replacing its positioning behavior, not classified dead.",
    "Move ownership: normalize rendered fragment coordinates in the existing pagination read; keep headless layout coordinates and canonical model selection unchanged. Dependency packaging remains provisional.",
    "Replace architecture: reject a reduced mode enum and parallel VirtualizedEditable families as public targets; no height-tree/store rewrite earns acceptance from this probe."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Three same-thread candidates; no independent workers or cross-model judge. 111 bounded rows reviewed: 50 delete, 6 localize, 28 retain, 27 runtime-gated; no missing dedicated declarations, unrelated nested editor algorithms excluded from the deletion audit. Proposed raw/Plate callers compile. The 100-block production browser packet completed but captured authored inputs changed; it is diagnostic only. The 1001 attempt was interrupted after preflight drift; stress was not run. Frozen end-position coverage exceeds the runner start/middle coverage. No consolidated implementation, current-source speed, native Find UI, accessibility, print, IME/device, collaboration or packed dependency acceptance.",
